linux-apfs-rw: read software-encrypted volumes, read-only (linuxfs)

Hooks crypt.c and unlock.c (components/linux-apfs/src) into the driver: a pass= mount option (the password,
in hex) unlocks the volume at mount, in place of the warning that it may not read correctly; object blocks are
decrypted as read when their checksum says so; file data is read through apfs_read_folio_encrypted(); and
whole-dstream reads (xattrs, compressed resource forks) decrypt each block by its extent's crypto_id.

